<svelte:head><title>How frontlanejobs works & privacy</title></svelte:head>
<article class="wrap prose-page"><span class="section-label">Clear sources. Human decisions.</span><h1>A clearer path<br />to good work.</h1><p class="lead">frontlanejobs brings frontend opportunities for India into one focused workspace.</p>
  <h2>How listings get here</h2><p>The board combines a researched starter collection with public employer feeds from Greenhouse, Lever and SmartRecruiters. We link directly to the original application page. We do not represent employers or guarantee availability, compensation or replies.</p>
  <h2>What “checked” means</h2><p>Curated listings carry the date they were researched. Employer-feed listings carry the time their feed returned them. Discovery and employer posting dates are kept separate. A successful feed refresh verifies listings from that feed. Older freelance projects should always be rechecked at their source.</p>
  <h2>Refreshes and coverage</h2><p>Employer feeds refresh daily at 8 AM IST when deployment scheduling is enabled. <a href="/updates">Source status</a> shows the actual latest attempt and any failures. Our coverage is limited to the listed employers. An unavailable source keeps its last successful data rather than falsely closing jobs.</p>
  <h2>Your workspace is private</h2><p>Browsing requires no account. Saving applications and profile details uses Google sign-in. Each account can access only its own tracker and profile. frontlanejobs stores your entered job details, notes, answers and dates to sync them across sessions and devices. Public job listings never contain your private answers.</p>
  <h2>Public viewer counts</h2><p>The footer shows unique browsers since tracking began and browsers active within the last 90 seconds. An anonymous cookie remembers your browser for one year and renews while you visit. We store a random browser ID and its latest activity time for these counters. Extra tabs and reloads count once; clearing cookies or using another browser counts as a new viewer. Counts update every 30 seconds while a tab is visible.</p>
  <h2>You control the record</h2><p>You can edit or delete tracker entries, export your tracker as CSV and clear profile fields. “Applied” requires an application date and your confirmation or receipt. A link click alone is never treated as an application. Do not put passwords, identity documents or payment credentials in notes.</p>
  <h2>Free to explore</h2><p>frontlanejobs charges no fee to browse or track applications. External freelance platforms may charge their own proposal or membership fees. No purchases or proposals happen automatically here.</p>
  <h2>Built to stay useful</h2><p>We use shared feed ingestion, deduplication, indexed private records and cached public responses. We will measure and expand capacity as the audience grows.</p>
</article>
